                "retweet_count": 3,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Today I met with members of the American Counseling Association during their annual advocacy day on Capitol Hill.\n\nRepresenting more than 60,000 mental health counselors nationwide, @ACACounselors plays a vital role in strengthening our mental health workforce and supporting communities across the country. We discussed ways to bolster that workforce and improve online safety for children.\n\nIn Congress, I co-introduced the Youth Mental Health Research Act to advance research and treatment for adolescents. I also serve on the Energy & Commerce Committee\u2019s Data Privacy Working Group, where we are focused on enhancing children\u2019s safety online.",
                "text_lang": "en",
